PART 7 — Heap vs Stack Memory (The Root Concept)
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    JVM MEMORY                           │
│                                                         │
│  HEAP (Shared between ALL threads)                      │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │ • All objects created with "new" live here       │   │
│  │ • Singleton beans live here                      │   │
│  │ • Class-level fields live here                   │   │
│  │ • DANGER: if user data stored here               │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                                                         │
│  STACK (Private per thread — each thread has its own)   │
│  ┌────────────────┐  ┌────────────────┐                 │
│  │ Thread A Stack │  │ Thread B Stack │                 │
│  │ local var a=1  │  │ local var a=5  │  ← DIFFERENT!  │
│  │ local var b=X  │  │ local var b=Y  │  ← ISOLATED!   │
│  └────────────────┘  └────────────────┘                 │
│  Thread A CANNOT read Thread B's stack. Ever.           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

