UserCartBuilder	✅ Yes	Prototype	Stores cart items per user
PDFStatementGenerator	✅ Yes	Prototype	Stores statement data per user
FINAL — 3 Golden Rules
RULE 1:
Class fields  = Heap memory  = SHARED between threads
               → DANGEROUS if storing user-specific data
               → Use @Scope("prototype")

RULE 2:
Local variables = Stack memory = PRIVATE per thread
                → ALWAYS safe, automatically isolated
                → Singleton is fine

RULE 3:
Stateless class  (only repos/tools injected, all data local) = Singleton
Stateful class   (stores user data in fields)                = Prototype

Interview Line
"Singleton is safe when a class is stateless — all user data lives in local variables on the thread stack, which is private per thread. SpinTheWheelService is safe as singleton because gameEligibility and spinTheWheelUserRecord are local variables — not class fields. Prototype is needed when a class stores user-specific data as class-level fields. Without prototype, two concurrent users share the same object — last writer wins — causing Anubhav to get Rahul's receipt. In fintech, this is a critical data leak bug."



